return {h=5,w=66,cr=190,hc=20,bh=70,gr="medium",eg={"plant"},st={45,35,50,70,50,30},ab={{34,0},{20,0},{102,1}},genus={en="Bulb Pokémon",es="Pokémon Bulbo",pt="Pokémon Bulbo"},flavor={en={[17]="The leaves on its head are very bitter. Eating one of these leaves is known to refresh a tired body.",[18]="Since they prefer moist, nutrient-rich soil, the areas where Petilil live are known to be good for growing plants.",[21]="The leaves on its head grow right back even if they fall out. These bitter leaves refresh those who eat them.",[22]="The leaves on its head grow right back even if they fall out. These bitter leaves refresh those who eat them.",[23]="The leaves on its head are very bitter. Eating one of these leaves is known to refresh a tired body.",[24]="Since they prefer moist, nutrient-rich soil, the areas where Petilil live are known to be good for growing plants.",[25]="The leaves on its head are very bitter. Eating one of these leaves is known to refresh a tired body.",[26]="Since they prefer moist, nutrient-rich soil, the areas where Petilil live are known to be good for growing plants.",[27]="Although the leaves on its head are bitter enough to cause dizziness, they provide relief from weariness, even more so when boiled.",[28]="By pruning the leaves on its head with regularity, this Pokémon can be grown into a fine plump shape.",[29]="Some say if you dry the leaves on its head, boil them down, and drink the infusion, your vigor will return, so Petilil is popular with the elderly.",[30]="They prefer clean water and soil. When the environment they live in turns bad, the whole bunch will up and move to a new area.",[33]="Petilil appears around sources of clean water. Boiling leaves from this Pokémon’s head results in a liquid that’s sometimes used as a bug repellent.",[34]="The deeper the color of a Petilil’s leaves, the healthier the Pokémon is. Petilil sometimes makes its home in a well-tended field or flowerbed.",[39]="The leaves on its head are highly valued for medicinal purposes. Dry the leaves in the sun, boil them, and then drink the bitter decoction for remarkably effective relief from fatigue."},es={[23]="Mordisquear las hojas de su cabeza permite recuperar toda la vitalidad, a pesar de que están muy amargas.",[24]="Habita tierras húmedas ricas en nutrientes donde la cosecha es abundante.",[25]="Mordisquear las hojas de su cabeza permite recuperar toda la vitalidad, a pesar de que están muy amargas.",[26]="Habita tierras húmedas ricas en nutrientes donde la cosecha es abundante.",[27]="Las hojas de su cabeza son tan amargas que casi producen náuseas, pero tienen un efecto revitalizante, sobre todo en forma de infusión.",[28]="Adquiere un aspecto esplendoroso cuando se le recortan las hojas de la cabeza con cierta asiduidad.",[29]="Los ancianos aprecian las hojas de su cabeza, ya que, secadas al sol y tomadas en infusión, devuelven la vitalidad perdida.",[30]="Prefiere el agua y la tierra sin impurezas. Si el entorno en el que habita empeora, emigra en grupo hacia un nuevo territorio.",[33]="Aparece en lugares de aguas limpias. La decocción de las hojas de su cabeza se puede utilizar como repelente de insectos.",[34]="Cuanto más sano está este Pokémon, más intenso se vuelve el color de sus hojas. A veces se asienta en huertos o jardines de flores bien cuidados."},pt="As folhas de sua cabeça são muito valorizadas para fins medicinais. Seque as folhas ao sol, ferva-as e beba o chá amargo para um alívio muito eficaz do cansaço."},evo={{s=548},{s=549,from=548,c={{t="use-item",item=80},{t="use-item",item=80,region=9}}}},moves={[11]={1,71,4,74,8,73,10,79,13,72,17,235,19,345,22,78,26,202,28,312,31,270,35,412,37,494,40,241,44,495,46,437},[14]={1,71,4,74,8,73,10,79,13,72,17,235,19,345,22,78,26,202,28,312,31,270,35,412,37,494,40,241,44,495,46,437},[15]={1,71,4,74,8,73,10,79,13,72,17,235,19,345,22,78,26,202,28,312,31,270,35,412,37,494,40,241,44,495,46,437},[16]={1,71,4,74,8,73,10,79,13,72,17,235,19,345,22,78,26,202,28,312,3